04-Governance-Framework

Section 1: Executive Summary
 This framework governs the organization's use of GitHub CoPilot, an AI-powered coding assistant developed by GitHub (Microsoft) that integrates directly into developer environments including Visual Studio Code, Visual Studio, JetBrains IDEs, Neovim, and the GitHub mobile application. CoPilot uses large language models trained on public and licensed code to suggest, generate, and explain code as developers write it. It can complete single lines or entire functions, answer natural-language questions about a codebase, generate tests, and independently carry out scoped engineering tasks with minimal developer supervision. CoPilot is being adopted to improve developer productivity and reduce time spent on routine, boilerplate, and repetitive coding tasks, allowing engineers to stay in flow, accelerate code review cycles, and offload well-defined background tasks to AI agents.

Section 2: Governance Structure (RACI)

Role: Business Owner - Responsibilty: Owns the business use case for CoPilot; justifies the productivity need, sponsors the budget, and accepts residual business risk.

Role: AI Governance Lead - Responsibility: Chairs overall governance oversight; coordinates cross-functional review, maintains the control framework, and tracks remediation of findings.

Role: Privacy (Data Protection Officer) - Responsibility: Reviews data flows for PII/customer data exposure, approves data handling practices, and oversees annual privacy impact assessments.

Role: Security (CISO/Security Engineering) - Responsibility: Reviews and approves security controls, secrets management, code scanning, and prompt-injection/ MCP-related exposure. 

Role: Platform Owner ( IT/ Engineering Operations) - Responsibility: Administers the GitHub Enterprise Admin Center, manages seat provisioning/deprovisioning, and maintains platform configuration.

Role: Legal/ Compliance Officer: - Responsibility: Reviews regulatory applicability, ensures Data Processing Agreements are current, and signs off on AI usage policy.

Role: Engineering Managers/ Tech Leads - Responsibilty: Enforce mandatory peer review of AI-generated code and supervise day-to-day responsible use within their teams.

Role: Executive Leadership/ Communications - Responsibility: Owns reputational accountability and external communication in the event of an AI-related incident. 

Section 3: Risk Tiering

-Assigned Tier: HIGH RISK-

GitHub CoPilot is classified as a high risk for the following reasons:

-It processes source code, and potentially customer data, credentials, or regulated information, if it appears in code, comments, or test files, and transmits that content to external cloud infratructure for inference.
-Its agentic workflows can autonomously plan and execute development tasks with reduced human supervision, meeting the high risk criterion.
-Organizations in regulated industries face direct compliance exposure when regulated data passes through the platform.
- a security failure (leaked secrets, injected vulnerable code, or a prompt-injection attack via a connected MCP/Extension) could lead to production compromise, not just an isolated productivity inconvenience.

This High Risk classification does not prohibit use; it determines that CoPilot must pass through the full approval process below, with mandatory Security and Privacy review; and must remain subject to the enhanced control set defined in Sections 5 and 6, including mandatory human code review, content exclusions, and enterprise data-processing safeguards.

